[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/952090297","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/5966#issuecomment-952090297","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/5966","id":952090297,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs44v765","user":{"login":"nateprewitt","id":5271761,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzE3NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5271761?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt","html_url":"https://github.com/nateprewitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-26T16:07:15Z","updated_at":"2021-10-26T16:07:15Z","body":"Hi @nniehoff, \r\n\r\nCould you clarify what you find misleading? The docstring at the top of the certs module reads:\r\n\r\n> This module returns the preferred default CA certificate bundle. There is only one — the one from the certifi package.\r\n\r\nThe functionality is pretty clearly documented and `requests.certs.where` is just an alias for certifi's `where`. That method is only intended to find the certifi cacert.pem file and doesn't provide any functionality for looking up other certs.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/952090297/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/952097360","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/5966#issuecomment-952097360","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/5966","id":952097360,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs44v9pQ","user":{"login":"nniehoff","id":14947575,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTQ3NTc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14947575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff","html_url":"https://github.com/nniehoff","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nniehoff/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-26T16:15:27Z","updated_at":"2021-10-26T16:15:27Z","body":"Sure, I completely expect the certifi package to return the cacerts bundle that is bundled with it.  However, IMO `requests.certs.where` isn't querying the certifi package but it is querying the requests package.  I would expect `requests.certs.where` to return the actual path the requests module is using.  In my case the value of the `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` but looking at [this](https://github.com/psf/requests/blob/b0e025ade7ed30ed53ab61f542779af7e024932e/requests/sessions.py#L718-L719) I believe it could also be the value of the `CURL_CA_BUNDLE`  environment variable.  \r\n\r\nI guess my suggestion would be `requests.certs.where` should override `certifi.where` and return either of the variables if set or default to the value of `certifi.where`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/952097360/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/952108592","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/5966#issuecomment-952108592","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/5966","id":952108592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs44wAYw","user":{"login":"nateprewitt","id":5271761,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzE3NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5271761?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt","html_url":"https://github.com/nateprewitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nateprewitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-26T16:27:33Z","updated_at":"2021-10-26T16:28:41Z","body":"Ok, thanks for clarifying. So it seems our documentation and the functionality is consistent, this is just a feature request for additional behavior. The proposal is a deviation from the current documented behavior that will likely negatively affect anyone using this specifically for `certifi`'s location.\r\n\r\nGiven that the feature is easily done with ~5 lines of Python locally, I'd advise writing a quick helper function for that for the time being. We may reconsider this if we release a new major version, but I'm going to close this for now since I don't think we'll see a change to this in the near future.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/952108592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]